## 7. Your data, credentials and responsibility

The Software runs on Your machine and acts on Your Centra Instance using API credentials that **You** supply and control. In particular, You acknowledge and agree that:

(a) the Software can read — and, where You enable write access, create, modify and delete — live commercial data in Your Centra Instance, including orders, prices and stock levels, whether in test or production environments; write access and production-environment access are disabled by default and operate only if and to the extent You enable them;

(b) actions initiated through the Software by an AI assistant, agent or other client connected to it are treated as Your actions. **You are solely responsible for the permissions You configure (including write access and production access), for the instructions given to any AI assistant connected to the Software, for reviewing and verifying the results of any action taken through the Software, and for maintaining appropriate back-ups and safeguards for Your data**;

(c) the Software may store a local cache of data from Your Centra Instance (including an encrypted local analytics database) on Your machine. That data is Yours; You are responsible for securing the machines and accounts on which the Software runs and for deleting local data when no longer required;

(d) You are responsible for keeping Your API tokens confidential and for scoping them appropriately; and

(e) the Software transmits usage statistics to service providers acting on Centra's behalf as described in Section 7A (Usage statistics) and checks for updates as described in Section 7A.10 (Update checks); apart from that, it runs entirely on Your machines and transmits no other data to Centra by virtue of this Licence. Data exchanged between the Software and Your Centra Instance is governed by the agreement (including any data processing terms) under which that Centra Instance is provided, not by this Licence, and Centra does not act as Your processor under this Licence. Where You connect an AI assistant or other client to the Software, data retrieved from Your Centra Instance — which may include personal data of Your customers — will be disclosed to that assistant and its providers; You are solely responsible, as controller or otherwise, for the lawfulness of that disclosure and for Your arrangements with those providers.

## 7A. Usage statistics

The Software records statistics about its own use and transmits them as described in this Section: usage statistics containing no personal data such as names or email addresses. This Section serves as the privacy notice for that processing and is published as part of this Licence. Centra is the controller of the processing described in this Section.

**7A.1 What is collected.** The usage statistics consist exclusively of: (a) the hostname of the Centra Instance to which the Software connects, and the brand (client) identifier and environment classification derived from that hostname; (b) a randomly generated installation identifier stored on Your machine; (c) session identifiers generated by the Software; (d) the version of the Software; (e) the operating system and processor architecture of the machine on which the Software runs; (f) the channel through which the Software was installed and the mode in which it is configured (configuration file or environment variables); (g) the name and version of the client application (for example, an AI assistant host) connected to the Software, and the version of the connection protocol it uses; (h) the type of each recorded action (for example a tool invocation, a session start or stop, an environment switch, or a playbook or guide retrieval), the names of the tools, playbooks and guides invoked, the surface through which they were invoked, their business-domain categories, and whether the invoked tool reads or writes data; (i) invocation outcomes — success or failure, duration, and a coarse error category; (j) the names, never the values, of request parameters; (k) the categories of Centra API permission used; (l) the permission mode (read-only or read-and-write); (m) true/false indicators of Centra-internal usage; and (n) the date and time of each recorded action and of the start of the session in which it occurred, and technical identifiers generated by the Software to de-duplicate transmissions. The Software determines the indicators in (m) locally — from known Centra-internal hostname patterns, an explicit staff-machine setting, and by checking whether the API token's contact email address is a Centra staff address — and transmits only the true/false results.

**7A.2 What is never collected.** The usage statistics never include message content, request or response payloads, raw error text, names, email addresses, IP addresses (which the recipient does not record), or any personal data of Your customers.

**7A.3 Local recording; usage recorded before transmission is enabled.** The Software records usage statistics locally on Your machine from installation. The local store retains at most approximately 30 days of records. When transmission is or becomes enabled, the transmitted usage statistics may include usage recorded before transmission was enabled, to the extent it remains in the local store, as well as usage occurring while transmission is enabled.

**7A.4 Deferred delivery.** If Your network prevents transmission, recorded usage statistics are retained locally — again, for at most approximately 30 days — and transmitted when a connection is available. Blocking the transmission endpoint therefore defers delivery rather than preventing it. To stop the transmission of usage statistics, disable them as described in Section 7A.5.

**7A.5 Your choice at installation; how to change it.** Whether the Software transmits usage statistics is Your choice, made when You install the Software or first accept this version of the Licence. Until You have made that choice, the Software transmits no usage statistics. You may enable or disable them at any time by any of the following means: running `centra-mcp setup telemetry --usage-stats=true` or `centra-mcp setup telemetry --usage-stats=false`; setting the `CENTRA_USAGE_STATISTICS` environment variable to `true` or `false`, for installations configured through environment variables; ticking or unticking the usage-statistics checkbox presented at installation or in the configuration screen of a host application; or using the usage-statistics setting in the Software's own setup interface. Disabling stops the transmission of usage statistics. The Software continues to record them locally within the retention bound described in Section 7A.3, and re-enabling transmits what remains in the local store (Section 7A.3).

**7A.6 Legal basis; Your right to object.** Centra processes the usage statistics on the basis of its legitimate interests in understanding how the Software is used, prioritising its development, and detecting defects. **You have the right to object to this processing at any time.** You exercise that right by disabling usage statistics as described in Section 7A.5, which stops their transmission to Centra; no other step is required.

**7A.7 Recipients.** The usage statistics are transmitted to a product-analytics service provider processing usage statistics on Centra's behalf in data centres within the European Union. The identity of the current provider is stated in the technical documentation published with the Software and may change from time to time without amendment of this Licence; the category described in the first sentence of this Section 7A.7 is the operative term.

**7A.8 Retention.** Transmitted usage statistics are retained for up to two years. Thereafter only aggregate data, from which the identifiers described in Section 7A.1 have been removed, is retained.

**7A.9 Identifier reset; access and erasure.** Deleting the installation-identifier file that the Software stores on Your machine causes a new installation identifier to be generated, dissociating future usage statistics from those already transmitted; it does not delete data already transmitted. You may request access to, or erasure of, the transmitted usage statistics associated with Your installation by writing to legal@centra.com.

**7A.10 Update checks.** The Software periodically checks whether a newer version of the Software is available by requesting the current release information from the distribution service through which Centra publishes the Software. That request carries the version of the Software in use and none of the usage statistics described in Section 7A.1; it is not affected by Your choice under Section 7A.5. As with any download, the operator of the distribution service may record the network address from which the request is made. Once a newer version has been available for more than seven days, or when the check has not succeeded for seven days, the Software requires an update before it continues to connect to Your Centra Instance.

